@startuml 07_cache_line_ping_pong
title 7. Why one shared counter is slow: the cache line moves between cores
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
autonumber

participant "Core 1\n(Thread A)" as C1
participant "Core 2\n(Thread B)" as C2
participant "Cache line\ncontaining x" as L

C1 -> L: lock add x (needs the line)
note over C1: Core 1 now owns the line\n(MESI state: Modified)
C2 -> L: lock add x (needs the line)
L -> C1: invalidate your copy
C1 --> L: line handed over
note over C2: Core 2 owns it now,\nCore 1 has nothing
C1 -> L: lock add x (wants it back)
L -> C2: invalidate your copy
C2 --> L: line handed over

note over L
  Each increment may need the line moved from another core.
  MESI = Modified / Exclusive / Shared / Invalid, the states
  a cache line can be in on each core.
  This transfer cost caps total throughput (Experiment 5).
end note
@enduml
